# Social

Rationale and delivery plan: [`docs/social.md`](../../docs/social.md).

## One place

Social has one place: a **group challenge** — a private, time-boxed,
invite-link contest over a shared goal. Built by extending the existing `Match`
primitive: host, invite token, metric, scoring mode, window, capped
participants, standings, lazy settlement.

Do not add a follow graph, an activity feed, comments, clubs, or a public group
directory.

A **crew** is a saved roster, not a place. It may appear in the create flow and
in a management list, and nowhere else. A crew has no feed, no board, no home
surface, and no notifications of its own — if it grows one it has become a
club. Crews are saved from a finished contest, never assembled from scratch.

## Consent

Members seated from a crew are pending until they open the contest: no scoring,
no nudges, greyed in standings. Any member may leave a crew, not just its
owner, and leaving blocks re-adding. The person being added holds the veto.

Enforce both structurally, not by convention. Leaving sets `CrewMember.leftAt`
so the unique key blocks re-adding; do not hard-delete the row. Pending members
get no progress entry in `computeStandings`, so passing their events in cannot
score them, and `days_completed` must not even query a pending member's
challenge rows.

## Identity

`User.name`, `UserProfile.displayName`, and the `publicNameFor` pseudonym are
the identity strings that exist. Do not add a fourth without an explicit product
decision.

If usernames ever ship they are a **lookup key, displayed nowhere**, resolved by
exact match only — no search, no autocomplete, no directory — rate-limited, and
opt-in with a default of false.

## Surface

- No fifth tab. Groups live under the Challenges tab as a segment.
- One primary action per screen.
- Reuse the `MatchBoardScreen` layout, but not its chrome — the match card kit
  drifted from the app (see "Visual consistency" in `docs/social.md`). Group
  lists and standings are divider lists matching `LeaderboardScreen` and
  `ChallengesScreen`, not per-row cards.
- Reactions are one tap and finite (cheer, nudge). No free text in group UI.

## Score

Group score derives from work the member already logs — `UserChallenge`
completions for `days_completed` (all of them, or only those of the contest's
activity when the host narrowed the scope), `MatchAttempt` for the
attempt-driven modes, plus the member's own tracked walks (`DeviceActivityLog`)
for a walk contest. Never require a second log of the same activity.

Only sensor-measured work scores. A hand-confirmed walk stays out of the
standings: a score anybody can type is not one the rest of the group can trust.

`computeStandings` takes an accumulator and ranks every mode the same way:
score first, then who reached that score first. Add a mode by adding a fold
step, never a parallel ranking function.

`cumulative_total` caps what one day contributes, per metric
(`MATCH_CUMULATIVE_DAILY_CAP_BY_METRIC`). Volume modes must not reward grinding
a single session.

Which modes a metric can run lives in `MATCH_MODES_BY_METRIC`; the client
filters to it and the contract rejects the rest. A new metric is entries in the
contract maps plus `match-metric.ts` on mobile — never a hardcoded activity
name in a screen.

How short a contest a mode can run lives in `MATCH_MIN_DAYS_BY_SCORING_MODE`,
and the shortcut tiles (`MATCH_WINDOWS_BY_SCORING_MODE`) are derived from it.
The client filters to them and the contract rejects the rest; do not restate
the matrix or add a second rule for custom lengths.

A length is a preset `window` or a `durationDays` count, never both. One
resolver (`resolveMatchLength`) turns either into a `MatchLength`, so no
caller carries a precedence rule.

New scoring modes need a product decision, not a convenient addition.

## Privacy

- Display name inside a group; pseudonym on the global leaderboard
  (`publicNameFor`). Do not leak one into the other.
- A group is defined by an activity, never a health category. `days_completed`
  counts any finished daily occurrence by default (`dailyScope: any_challenge`),
  so a board cannot imply a diagnosis. A host may narrow it to the contest's own
  activity (`chosen_activity`), which scopes by `Challenge.deviceMetric` — an
  activity, still never a category. Do not bind a group to one named challenge
  without revisiting that.
- Standings carry a name and a score. No category, no vitals, no challenge
  history from outside the group.
- Invite-only. No discovery, no public listing.

## Lifecycle

Every group has an end. Settlement stays lazy-on-read; do not introduce a
background settler. Re-engagement is "Run it back", not an open-ended club.

## Notifications

At most one group push per group per day, plus the settlement result. Cheers and
nudges are rate-limited and idempotent on `(groupId, fromUserId, toUserId, day)`.

## Contract

Additive changes only — new enum values and optional fields. Store clients
linger and `oasdiff` must stay green.
